# Secrets - NEVER commit (Appendix A + rule #39/#40)
.env
credentials.json
token.json
*.pem
*.key
# Quarantined credential values awaiting revocation (docs/SECURITY.md)
SECRETS-TO-REVOKE.local.md
*.local.md

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# Test / lint caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Runtime scratch ONLY.
#
# The four lifecycle artifacts per game - declaration, config, log, result -
# are NOT scratch and must be committed: App. F Mandatory Rules #4 requires
# every game's config file in the repository, and rule #50 wants the set, so a
# grader can replay a match instead of taking our word for it. They used to be
# excluded wholesale by `results/*.json` + `logs/*.json`, which meant the repo
# could never contain a single piece of evidence that a game had been played.
#
# What genuinely is scratch: half-written files, the crash-recovery checkpoint
# (evidence for us, never a document the league reads - see services/
# series_guard.py), and superseded run directories.
*.tmp
rows_checkpoint.json
*.superseded-*

# The lecturer's own course materials (assignment PDF + submission guidelines).
# They are read constantly and cited throughout docs/, but this repo is split
# into two PUBLIC role repos, and republishing someone else's copyrighted
# course documents twice over is not ours to do. Keep them on disk, cite them
# by name in docs/, never track them (docs/TODO.md 11.5.11).
instruction/*.pdf

# Local sync scratch (git bundles used to mirror the dev environment)
.sync/

# Local agent workspace
.claude/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# results
#
# Generated output is ignored by NAME, never as a whole directory. Blanket
# `results/` (2026-08-16) also swallowed the league lifecycle artifacts -
# declaration, config, log, result - which are graded deliverables written to
# results/friendly_<game_id>/ by the series driver. Under that pattern
# `git add results/` adds nothing and says nothing, so a counted series would
# be submitted with no evidence beside it. Name the noise instead.
results/rehearsal*/
results/*demo*
.env.save
